WEBVTT

00:00.870 --> 00:16.640
Welcome to this online course on programming,
I am Shankar Balachandran from the Computer

00:16.640 --> 00:20.690
Science Engineering Department at IIT, Madras.

00:20.690 --> 00:26.190
This course is designed in such a way that
it can be spread across 5 weeks and you are

00:26.190 --> 00:30.060
going to have about 2 lectures every week.

00:30.060 --> 00:37.810
So, total of 10 lectures and this course is
also designed in such a way that you can take

00:37.810 --> 00:46.180
this in 15 minute chunks called modules and
you would be given a small practice test,

00:46.180 --> 00:47.309
right after the every module.

00:47.309 --> 00:49.829
So, let us jump right into the course.

00:49.829 --> 00:54.219
So, before getting into programming we need
to understand little bit about what computers

00:54.219 --> 00:55.460
are about.

00:55.460 --> 01:01.809
What you are seeing in this picture here is
ENIAC the, so called first digital computer,

01:01.809 --> 01:04.110
which was build in the 1940s.

01:04.110 --> 01:11.430
And you can see how huge it is, it is almost
like house in size, it was massive compared

01:11.430 --> 01:16.260
to the modern personal computer standards
by no means ENIAC can be called the personal

01:16.260 --> 01:25.020
computer, it had 17,000 vacuum tubes, 5 million
hand solder joints, it weighed quite a bit

01:25.020 --> 01:31.710
and it is use consumed 150 kilo watts of power,
no way this would be a personal computer.

01:31.710 --> 01:40.540
However, June 2, 2000 what you seeing on this
picture is a micro photograph of Pentium 4

01:40.540 --> 01:47.680
and it was designed in the year 2000 and deployed
in the market, it could run at 1.5 gigahertz.

01:47.680 --> 01:53.490
That means, it can do 1.5 billion operations
per second, it had 42 million transistors

01:53.490 --> 01:56.230
as opposed to this puny ENIAC.

01:56.230 --> 02:02.530
And it was build in this technology called
0.18 micron technology, which means the transistors

02:02.530 --> 02:07.390
and the gates that were used to design as
small as 0.18 micron.

02:07.390 --> 02:15.129
So, in the 40 or 50 years computers have moved
quite far away from the first notion of digital

02:15.129 --> 02:16.129
computer.

